WEBVTT

00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:02.875
- Previously on The O. C:
- You drink a lot?

00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:04.750
I guess. I mean, what's a lot?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.667
Have you ever had so much to drink
that you blacked out?

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:11.292
How much is the Land Trust
offering me for Balboa Heights?

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.667
That's it?
That's your whole dog-and-pony show?

00:00:13.917 --> 00:00:15.833
- What are you doing Saturday?
- What are you doing Saturday?

00:00:16.042 --> 00:00:19.542
- I have a date with Summer.
- What are you doing Friday night?

00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:30.375
So, what's it gonna be, huh?

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:34.792
You want your menorah or
a candy cane? Christmas or Hanukkah?

00:00:37.458 --> 00:00:41.083
Don't worry about it, buddy, because
in this house, you don't have to choose.

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:45.542
Allow me to introduce you
to a little something I like to call...

00:00:46.042 --> 00:00:48.167
...Chrismukkah.
- Chrismukkah?

00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:50.667
That's right.
The new holiday sweeping the nation.

00:00:50.875 --> 00:00:53.083
- Hey, fellas, we got the tree.
- Hey.

00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:56.333
- Or at least the living room.
- Guys, a little help.

00:00:56.542 --> 00:00:59.875
I saved a spot for you right there.
Put your muscle into it.

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:02.333
Excellent. To the right a little.
Don't hurt it.

00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:04.458
Those needles are brittle.
That's perfect.

00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:09.208
You guys, you guys. A-plus. A-plus.
I love the holidays. I love them all.

00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:12.417
- We didn't really know how to raise Seth.
- So I raised myself.

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:15.750
In doing so, I created the greatest
superholiday known to mankind...

00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:19.792
...drawing on the best that Christianity
and Judaism have to offer.

00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:21.708
And you call it Chrismukkah?

00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:26.125
Just hearing you say it makes me feel
all festive. Allow me to elaborate.

00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:30.375
You see, for my father here, a poor,
struggling Jew growing up in the Bronx...

00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:32.375
...Christmas meant
Chinese food and a movie.

00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:34.667
For my mom here,
Waspy McWasp...

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:37.458
...well, it meant a tree,
stockings and all the trimmings.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.375
- Isn't that right?
- We're very proud.

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:40.833
- I'm not a Wasp.
- Sure.

00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:44.958
Highlights include eight days of presents
followed by one of many presents.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:46.833
So, what do you think?

00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:50.833
- Sounds great for you guys.
- For you too.

00:01:51.042 --> 00:01:54.042
Hey, dip a toe in the Chrismukkah pool.
There's room for all of us.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.542
Isn't there an Atwood family tradition
you'd like to incorporate...

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.958
...into Seth's  Êber-holiday?
- Yeah.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.667
Atwood and holidays
is not a good combination.

00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:07.208
- What did you guys do?
- No, seriously, thanks, but...

00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.500
Come on, man,
there's got to be something.

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:13.375
My holiday memories pretty much
consist of my mom drunk...

00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:15.333
...and me getting my ass kicked.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.167
Well, this year will be entirely different.

00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:23.042
New memories. It'll be great.

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:26.792
Yeah. Well, I'll do
whatever you want me to.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.167
That's the spirit. Come here.

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:36.083
- Oy humbug.
- It's a big holiday for anyone.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.333
Yeah, I'm still wrapping my head
around it. Give him some time.

00:02:39.542 --> 00:02:41.917
Why don't we trim the tree?

00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:46.250
You know what, you guys? Soon Ryan
will learn the magic of Chrismukkah.

00:02:46.417 --> 00:02:49.792
Worry not. I will convert him.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:35.958
I was gone five minutes.
How did this turn into Santa's workshop?

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:39.375
I see someone took down the wreath
I hung on the door.

00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:41.250
It fell. What are you wrapping?

00:03:41.458 --> 00:03:44.833
Two Seth Cohen starter packs. We got
Death Cab, Bright Eyes, The Shins...

00:03:45.042 --> 00:03:46.625
...Kavalier &amp; Clay and Goonies.

00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:50.542
It's not just for kids, Ryan, it's not.
I don't care what they tell you.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.292
Summer and Anna
are gonna love them both equally.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.083
You're getting them the same thing?

00:03:55.292 --> 00:03:58.042
Yes, I am. Sometimes I'm so crafty,
I surprise myself.

00:03:58.208 --> 00:03:59.792
No good can come of this,
you know that.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.250
Nope, I don't.

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:03.208
- You're gonna have to choose, man.
- Hey.

00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:06.667
Not on Chrismukkah, I don't. Okay?
There's no choosing in Chrismukkah.

00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:10.250
- Well, you didn't get me anything, right?
- No.

00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.417
Come on, man, lighten up.

00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:20.375
Okay, fine. Stay dark. Dark works too.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.583
- Oh, Ryan, what is your shoe size?
- Why?

00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:32.917
- No reason.
- Might that be a Chrismukkah list?

00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:34.708
- No. Why do you ask?
- Okay.

00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:37.667
- Let me just see it, then, real fast.
- It's work.

00:04:37.875 --> 00:04:40.833
- I love your work. It fascinates me.
- I thought you said no gifts.

00:04:41.042 --> 00:04:45.167
- Well, we did. As in, no gifts for us.
- All right. All right.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.458
Well, Chrismukkah's ruined.

00:04:48.208 --> 00:04:50.542
Don't even say it. It's unruinable.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.833
It's got twice the resistance
of any normal holiday.

00:04:53.042 --> 00:04:55.542
Your father refused our settlement offer.
He wants a trial.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.667
That's not what he said yesterday.
He said if you met his offer...

00:04:58.875 --> 00:05:01.333
As of this morning,
Scrooge wants to go to court...

00:05:01.542 --> 00:05:04.667
...which means I have to spend
the holidays preparing for trial.

00:05:04.875 --> 00:05:06.000
Because with Rachel
out...

00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:10.333
Chrismukkah is ruined. Sooner or later
we will get through a holiday around here.

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:11.625
Stop it right now, okay?

00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:15.958
Don't give up on the miracle that is
Chrismukkah. What is happening to you...?

00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:21.042
You'll see. You'll see too.
You'll all see. You'll all see.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.583
- You're starting to scare me.
- I'm okay with that.

00:05:23.792 --> 00:05:28.083
Okey-dokey, here we go.
Which tie? What are you thinking?

00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:32.208
This one? All right? Or...

00:05:32.417 --> 00:05:36.000
- The second one, definitely.
- All right.

00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:40.375
- So you have a job interview today?
- It's just a meet and greet.

00:05:40.583 --> 00:05:44.083
But we gotta dress for success, right?

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.042
Look, I'm working on it, kiddo.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:52.000
I'll find a job. I know there's a lot
of extra pressure on the holidays.

00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:53.833
There doesn't have to be pressure...

00:05:54.042 --> 00:05:58.083
...because there doesn't have to be
any holidays. Really.

00:05:58.292 --> 00:06:01.042
- What do you mean?
- We can skip Christmas. It's not like...

00:06:01.208 --> 00:06:05.417
...it's not gonna happen again next year,
and holidays just make people depressed.

00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:08.750
Are you? Depressed?

00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:11.792
You were supposed to go
to therapy after Mexico. We never...

00:06:11.958 --> 00:06:14.250
- I'm great. I'm just saying.
- Okay. Good.

00:06:14.458 --> 00:06:17.542
Because we're not skipping
Christmas. Come on.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.042
I'll find a job, we'll figure out
a way to make this whole thing work...

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.792
...and we're gonna have
lots to celebrate about, okay?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.917
Come on. Skipping Christmas.

00:06:27.125 --> 00:06:30.167
- You sure about this tie?
- Yeah, definitely.

00:06:31.042 --> 00:06:33.208
- All right.
- You look great.

00:06:33.417 --> 00:06:35.958
Skipping Christmas.
What are you, the Grinch?

00:06:38.417 --> 00:06:41.083
So Summer and Anna
are both coming to this party?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.333
- But neither one's my date.
- They know that?

00:06:43.542 --> 00:06:45.417
Yeah, in theory they both know that.

00:06:45.792 --> 00:06:47.958
Come on, man, relax.
It's a big party, okay?

00:06:48.167 --> 00:06:50.583
You might be all doom and gloom,
but me? Check it out.

00:06:50.792 --> 00:06:53.542
I'm snowflakes. I'm latkes.
Chrismukkah is coming.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.667
And when Chrismukkah ends?

00:06:57.292 --> 00:06:59.875
- I hate when Chrismukkah ends.
- Cohen.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.292
Hi, Ryan. I wanted to know
what the deal was for tonight.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.708
If you were driving,
or should I pick you up?

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:08.875
Hey, Seth. So, what time
are you thinking for tonight?

00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:16.167
- Hey, Summer.
- Hey, Anna.

00:07:16.625 --> 00:07:20.958
You guys. I was thinking that
we should all probably meet there.

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:24.542
How about that? At whatever time
you choose, by whatever means.

00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:29.625
- Sounds great.
- Yeah. Perfect.

00:07:31.708 --> 00:07:34.292
You'd better pray
for a Chrismukkah miracle.

00:07:35.292 --> 00:07:37.708
I've got Jesus and Moses
on my side, man.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.667
Yeah, make sure all that
goes all the way around the bottom.

00:07:44.875 --> 00:07:49.333
Now, guys, the balls are the key
to the whole tree. They need to breathe.

00:07:51.917 --> 00:07:55.000
Hey, Kirsten, what do you think?

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:58.167
- It's really something.
- You don't like it?

00:07:58.375 --> 00:08:03.458
It's not that. It's just that my mom used
to put the Christmas tree in the foyer.

00:08:03.667 --> 00:08:07.333
- It's just a tradition that we have.
- Yeah, Caleb told me.

00:08:07.542 --> 00:08:10.375
But then I thought, "You know,
the holidays are hard enough."

00:08:10.542 --> 00:08:13.042
Your father doesn't need
to be reminded of the past.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.250
Caleb needs to enjoy this Christmas.

00:08:15.458 --> 00:08:17.792
And did Caleb tell you
we need to borrow your office?

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.542
We're doing the Santa thing for the kids,
and we need a holding area for the elves.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.125
What are you doing here?
Your father said...

00:08:23.292 --> 00:08:25.375
...you're working from home.
- He did?

00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:27.958
He's just
full of surprises.

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:33.375
I changed my mind. If the Land Trust
can come up with $200 million...

00:08:33.542 --> 00:08:36.292
...then surely they can come up
with $300 million.

00:08:36.458 --> 00:08:38.000
I thought this was over.

00:08:38.208 --> 00:08:40.208
You can always get more blood
from the stone.

00:08:40.417 --> 00:08:42.667
But the stone is my husband.

00:08:42.875 --> 00:08:44.708
Let's spend the holidays working.

00:08:44.917 --> 00:08:48.667
- That sounds good. You have fun.
- What are you talking about?

00:08:48.875 --> 00:08:51.625
I'm gonna do something
that I haven't done in...

00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:53.833
...ever.

00:08:54.042 --> 00:08:57.833
- I'm taking Christmas vacation.
- Don't be ridiculous, Kiki.

00:08:58.042 --> 00:09:01.333
- You hate sitting around.
- Not as much as I hate fighting with you.

00:09:01.542 --> 00:09:03.875
So you spend two weeks
buried in legal documents.

00:09:04.083 --> 00:09:05.375
I'm gonna be wrapping gifts.

00:09:07.375 --> 00:09:11.667
- I hate Christmas.
- Well, Chrismukkah's not much better.

00:09:11.875 --> 00:09:14.833
You don't wanna know.
Holidays make what's bad even worse.

00:09:15.042 --> 00:09:16.500
I just wish my dad
would drop the act.

00:09:16.708 --> 00:09:19.208
I don't need it.
And I don't need Christmas.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.042
Who do you have to spend it with?

00:09:21.208 --> 00:09:23.875
Christmas Eve with my dad,
Christmas Day with my mom.

00:09:24.042 --> 00:09:26.958
Plus, she's making me go to a stupid
Newport Group party tonight.

00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:30.583
- The Cohens are going too, so...
- So at least we'll be miserable together.

00:09:31.042 --> 00:09:34.333
- Deal?
- Deal. So am I seeing you after school?

00:09:34.542 --> 00:09:38.083
I got some stuff to do,
some shopping. South Coast Plaza.

00:09:38.292 --> 00:09:41.333
You're going to South Coast Plaza?
Alone?

00:09:41.542 --> 00:09:42.667
I don't think
you're ready for that.

00:09:42.875 --> 00:09:45.167
You need a seasoned expert
to protect you.

00:09:45.917 --> 00:09:48.792
Well, you know someone?

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.583
So no luck, huh?

00:10:29.792 --> 00:10:32.458
There's a 99-cent store down the street.

00:10:34.042 --> 00:10:37.167
I guess I can't really afford
this place anymore.

00:10:37.375 --> 00:10:39.125
Why did we come?

00:10:40.542 --> 00:10:44.083
I know it sounds stupid,
but I like it here.

00:10:44.292 --> 00:10:46.958
Everything is so perfect.

00:10:47.167 --> 00:10:49.042
You walk around feeling
like your problems...

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.000
...can be solved by
the right nail polish...

00:10:52.167 --> 00:10:53.833
...or a new pair of shoes.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.583
Miss, I'm gonna have to ask
to see your purse.

00:11:01.792 --> 00:11:04.625
- Hey, what are you doing?
- I can't let you leave the premises.

00:11:04.792 --> 00:11:07.917
If you don't hand over your purse,
I'll have to call the police.

00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:09.500
Look, back off, all right?

00:11:09.708 --> 00:11:11.917
- Ryan, it's okay.
- No, it's not.

00:11:12.125 --> 00:11:13.875
Your purse. Now.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.958
What are you doing?

00:11:50.625 --> 00:11:52.333
What are you doing?
Working from home?

00:11:52.542 --> 00:11:54.667
- I'm on vacation.
- Yes. Clearly.

00:11:54.875 --> 00:11:58.583
- I find reviewing accounts to be relaxing.
- I hope that's a recessive gene.

00:11:58.833 --> 00:12:00.708
You should be so lucky.

00:12:00.917 --> 00:12:05.542
Look, I haven't taken a vacation
in a while, and I'm easing into it.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.583
- I don't judge. I only mock.
- That you get from your father.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.792
Oh, my God, they're coming in?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.750
Oh, the... I got you. What are those?

00:12:14.958 --> 00:12:18.125
They came for Ryan
from his mom and his brother.

00:12:19.125 --> 00:12:21.542
You know what he said
about the holidays?

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:24.583
When he talks like that,
I have no idea what to say.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.583
Me neither. You just have
to be yourself.

00:12:27.792 --> 00:12:29.250
Yeah, because that
always works so well.

00:12:29.417 --> 00:12:32.458
Being a family is hard
under any circumstance.

00:12:32.667 --> 00:12:37.375
Creating a new one?
That's gotta feel weird sometimes.

00:12:37.583 --> 00:12:40.333
Feeling weird is
right in my wheelhouse.

00:12:43.375 --> 00:12:46.750
What is it? Is Grandpa going crazy
with the company credit card again?

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.833
What is it this time? Hookers?
A little blow, perhaps?

00:12:50.042 --> 00:12:51.917
Grandpa likes to dance
with ye white lady?

00:12:52.125 --> 00:12:55.625
- What are you talking about?
- I don't know. What is it?

00:12:55.833 --> 00:12:57.208
It's... Hopefully, it's nothing.

00:12:57.417 --> 00:13:00.167
You should go get ready,
because we have to be there soon.

00:13:00.375 --> 00:13:01.917
I'll go put on my face.

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:14.875
Hi. This is Kirsten Cohen
from the Newport Group.

00:13:15.042 --> 00:13:19.083
My father ordered a survey of
the Balboa Heights and I've lost my copy.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:24.292
I really need to see the document.
Is it possible for you to fax it over to me?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.083
- I cannot believe this. Marissa?
- Julie.

00:13:34.292 --> 00:13:37.417
Look, I have to host the most important
event of my career tonight.

00:13:37.625 --> 00:13:39.458
At least your priorities are in order.

00:13:39.667 --> 00:13:43.125
You know, it's amazing how these
calamities keep happening on your watch.

00:13:43.333 --> 00:13:45.458
Oh, so I'm to blame for this one too?

00:13:45.667 --> 00:13:47.583
- Where did she learn to steal?
- Stop it.

00:13:47.958 --> 00:13:51.625
I'm the one who stole, remember?
I'm the one to blame, not Dad.

00:13:51.833 --> 00:13:55.000
Look, we're lucky the store
is not pressing charges.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:58.292
Okay? Marissa and I were deciding
what an appropriate punishment...

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:03.708
Oh, really? Well, way to rule with
the iron fist, Stalin, but it's not up to her.

00:14:03.917 --> 00:14:07.625
- No car, no allowance, no weekends.
- So I can stay home tonight?

00:14:07.833 --> 00:14:12.667
Starting tomorrow. I won't have my
party ruined by your little sticky fingers.

00:14:13.333 --> 00:14:18.917
Look, sweetie, I know that this time of
year makes everything bad seem worse.

00:14:19.125 --> 00:14:20.500
But why did you do this?

00:14:23.875 --> 00:14:26.417
I thought it would be...

00:14:26.958 --> 00:14:28.917
Look, I wasn't...

00:14:32.625 --> 00:14:33.625
It was stupid.

00:14:33.875 --> 00:14:35.708
I called the therapist
on the way over.

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:37.917
- Mom.
- She's right, kiddo.

00:14:38.125 --> 00:14:40.208
Therapy was part of the deal
of you moving in.

00:14:40.417 --> 00:14:43.708
Okay, look, I've been doing
way better since Mexico.

00:14:43.917 --> 00:14:46.750
4.0 first quarter.
Charity League, social chair.

00:14:46.917 --> 00:14:50.417
I scheduled you an appointment
tomorrow with Dr. Milano. He's great.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:54.708
I'm sorry, but I can handle it.

00:14:54.917 --> 00:14:58.708
This. L... I won't do it again, I promise.

00:14:59.458 --> 00:15:02.375
Honey, I love you.

00:15:04.792 --> 00:15:05.917
But I don't believe you.

00:15:08.083 --> 00:15:10.083
You might actually find it helpful.

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:13.583
Yeah. Whatever. I need to get ready.

00:15:13.792 --> 00:15:15.708
And, Mom, you have your
big party to throw.

00:15:15.917 --> 00:15:19.083
I'm sure you don't want to keep
Caleb waiting.

00:15:25.083 --> 00:15:26.958
Hey. What's up, man? You're back.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:32.875
So that's pretty cool, right?
Your mom and brother got you something.

00:15:33.083 --> 00:15:36.000
Yeah. Except now I have
a total of eight gifts to buy.

00:15:36.208 --> 00:15:37.583
I only saved enough for one.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:42.125
Ryan, that sort of reminds me
of the story of Hanukkah, dude.

00:15:42.333 --> 00:15:47.000
Check it out. The lamp... You know what?
I think you get the gist.

00:15:47.208 --> 00:15:50.958
- How was the mall?
- Weird.

00:15:51.833 --> 00:15:54.750
You've really painted a picture for me.
I feel like I was there.

00:15:54.958 --> 00:15:57.792
Marissa picked up a few things
without paying for them.

00:15:59.083 --> 00:16:01.458
- What? As in...
- Shoplifting.

00:16:01.792 --> 00:16:03.333
Yeah.

00:16:03.917 --> 00:16:06.333
- Yeah, that's weird.
- It's the time of year.

00:16:06.542 --> 00:16:09.083
And with everything that's going on
with her family...

00:16:09.292 --> 00:16:12.042
- Yeah, I'm sure it's gotta be hard for her.
- Yeah.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:16.583
I just wish there was something
I could do or say.

00:16:19.042 --> 00:16:20.125
Oh, I got you something.

00:16:20.333 --> 00:16:24.542
- No, no, no. We had an agreement.
- But this is different, this is a requirement.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:29.958
I know it's a bit minty, but, you know,
we all have one, so we just thought...

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.042
No, that's cool.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.167
Well, good. Maybe it'll meet
a kinder fate than your wreath did.

00:16:36.375 --> 00:16:38.750
But, if not, we still
wanted you to have it.

00:16:38.958 --> 00:16:40.708
- Thanks.
- All right.

00:16:40.958 --> 00:16:42.208
I'm gonna go
make magic happen.

00:16:42.417 --> 00:16:45.417
I feel like my hair's
working for me tonight.

00:16:55.417 --> 00:16:57.958
I'm late. I know. I know.

00:16:59.167 --> 00:17:01.917
I'll hurry.
You're not gonna believe this...

00:17:02.125 --> 00:17:04.583
...but your father and I
reached a settlement today.

00:17:04.792 --> 00:17:07.917
He gouged me a little.
Well, you know, he gouged me a lot.

00:17:08.125 --> 00:17:13.125
- He asked you for more money?
- Just $250 million.

00:17:13.333 --> 00:17:14.417
But we closed the deal.

00:17:14.625 --> 00:17:17.750
- He claims that he did it because of you.
- Is that what he told you?

00:17:17.958 --> 00:17:20.625
It seems your vacation
really hit him hard.

00:17:20.833 --> 00:17:24.750
Because he says he wants
to spend the holidays as a family.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:29.375
You know, maybe...
Maybe he's changing.

00:17:29.583 --> 00:17:34.625
Or maybe he is a truly fantastic liar.
What's wrong?

00:17:40.792 --> 00:17:42.083
I found something today.

00:17:42.417 --> 00:17:46.250
And I don't know if I can give it to you,
but I don't know if I can't.

00:17:46.458 --> 00:17:51.042
- Okay, well...
- He's gonna know that I gave this to you.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.917
And he's gonna have
every right to fire me.

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.375
You have got to be kidding me.

00:18:14.875 --> 00:18:16.250
This changes everything.

00:18:16.458 --> 00:18:20.500
And I'm gonna have to learn how to relax,
because I'm gonna have a lot of free time.

00:18:21.625 --> 00:18:26.042
- I'm sorry, honey.
- Not as sorry as he's gonna be.

00:18:27.708 --> 00:18:31.958
- You still wanna go to the party?
- I wouldn't miss it for the world.

00:18:48.792 --> 00:18:51.542
- Anna. Hey.
- Mistletoe.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.708
That's very festive of you.

00:18:55.917 --> 00:18:57.708
I thought we were meeting there.

00:18:57.917 --> 00:18:59.792
I was thinking maybe
we could go together.

00:19:00.042 --> 00:19:01.583
I would love to.
You know I would.

00:19:01.792 --> 00:19:03.625
But don't you think
that would violate...

00:19:03.833 --> 00:19:05.917
...our little Geneva Convention
of dating we have?

00:19:06.125 --> 00:19:08.250
Because I told Summer
I'd meet you both there.

00:19:08.458 --> 00:19:10.542
Well, how is Summer ever gonna know?

00:19:14.417 --> 00:19:17.583
- Mistletoe. What is she doing here?
- What are you doing here?

00:19:17.792 --> 00:19:20.167
- I thought we had a deal, Cohen.
- Which you violated.

00:19:20.375 --> 00:19:21.958
- As did you.
- She's got a point.

00:19:22.167 --> 00:19:25.375
- You're on her side?
- No. There are no sides, you guys.

00:19:25.583 --> 00:19:30.042
There's only rides. With my parents.
We'll all go together.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.042
- Fine.
- Fine.

00:19:48.042 --> 00:19:53.000
So I have a gift for you.
I'll give it to you later.

00:19:53.208 --> 00:19:58.750
I have a present for you too.
I'll also give it to you later.

00:19:58.958 --> 00:20:01.042
I can't wait.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.208
For either.

00:20:03.417 --> 00:20:05.042
For both.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.708
Seth, are you ready?
Come on, let's go.

00:20:09.667 --> 00:20:12.833
Hi, Summer. Anna.

00:20:13.042 --> 00:20:14.667
Ladies.

00:20:14.875 --> 00:20:16.500
Oh, this is gonna be some party.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:22.417
You know, maybe it's not
such a bad idea.

00:20:23.417 --> 00:20:25.250
What does that mean?

00:20:25.458 --> 00:20:27.500
It might be good
to have someone to talk to.

00:20:27.708 --> 00:20:31.208
- You're someone. I can't talk to you?
- You can talk to me, it's just...

00:20:31.417 --> 00:20:34.875
What? I need the help of a trained
professional because I stole a lipstick?

00:20:35.083 --> 00:20:38.958
- It's not about the lipstick.
- Then I guess I don't see what it's about.

00:20:39.917 --> 00:20:42.917
- You should do what you want.
- I will.

00:20:43.125 --> 00:20:46.417
If no one's making my parents
go to therapy, then no one's making me.

00:20:46.625 --> 00:20:49.875
You know, I'm the only
normal one in this family.

00:20:52.167 --> 00:20:53.708
Sorry.

00:20:55.667 --> 00:20:59.458
I think I left my wrap upstairs. Could you
grab it for me? I need to get my purse.

00:20:59.667 --> 00:21:01.500
Sure.

00:21:40.333 --> 00:21:42.500
Mushroom crescent?
Crab and brie phyllo?

00:21:42.708 --> 00:21:44.958
Come on, buddy.
Change it up a little bit.

00:21:45.167 --> 00:21:47.000
Enjoy the party.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:50.333
Come on, Seth. I'm going this way.

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.625
I'm going this way.

00:21:52.833 --> 00:21:56.583
Oh, you guys are?
I'm gonna go look for Ryan. Excuse me.

00:21:58.417 --> 00:22:00.500
Kirsten, Sandy, welcome.

00:22:00.708 --> 00:22:02.167
- Kiki.
- Hey.

00:22:02.417 --> 00:22:05.083
Great to see you.
Did Sandman give you our good news?

00:22:05.458 --> 00:22:07.250
- He did.
- I need to follow up...

00:22:07.417 --> 00:22:09.042
...on some things with you,
if you don't mind...

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:10.542
Come, Sanford, it's a party.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:13.917
Look back on your Berkeley days.
Maybe you can smoke the tree.

00:22:15.333 --> 00:22:17.417
Smoke the tree. Funny.

00:22:17.625 --> 00:22:19.625
I'm gonna nail him now.

00:22:20.583 --> 00:22:22.875
- So, what do you think?
- About?

00:22:23.083 --> 00:22:25.250
The party. You haven't said anything.
Like it?

00:22:25.458 --> 00:22:27.125
I mean, I know how you feel
about the tree...

00:22:27.333 --> 00:22:28.958
...but if you can get past that.

00:22:29.167 --> 00:22:30.958
- It's great.
- And what did Caleb think?

00:22:31.125 --> 00:22:35.083
- I mean, has he said anything to you?
- I haven't had a chance to talk to him.

00:22:35.333 --> 00:22:38.458
I just want this to be
a party that he'll never forget.

00:22:38.667 --> 00:22:41.083
I think you have a shot.

00:22:52.833 --> 00:22:54.958
- You okay?
- Yeah. Why?

00:22:55.583 --> 00:22:56.667
I don't know.

00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:58.667
Today's been kind of intense...

00:22:58.875 --> 00:23:01.542
...and I know you don't
really wanna be here.

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:04.708
I wanna be where you are,
and you're here, so...

00:23:06.875 --> 00:23:10.750
Marissa.
Oh, you wore the Chanel. How pretty.

00:23:10.958 --> 00:23:13.542
Ryan. You haven't said hello to Caleb yet.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:16.833
He was talking to other people,
and I didn't want to interrupt.

00:23:17.042 --> 00:23:18.875
- He's ready now, so...
- I'm not.

00:23:19.083 --> 00:23:20.833
- Marissa.
- Mom.

00:23:21.042 --> 00:23:23.458
- You are a guest at this party.
- You made me come.

00:23:23.667 --> 00:23:26.667
- You're in enough trouble.
- Then I guess I've got nothing to lose.

00:23:26.875 --> 00:23:30.125
- This is the way it's gonna be?
- I don't know. I'll ask my shrink.

00:23:31.958 --> 00:23:34.625
You know what,
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:39.708
- I hate the holidays.
- Right there with you.

00:23:44.333 --> 00:23:46.000
Caleb. You have time to talk?

00:23:46.208 --> 00:23:48.583
- No.
- Come on, make some.

00:23:51.833 --> 00:23:54.500
- What is this?
- A geological survey of the Heights...

00:23:54.667 --> 00:23:58.167
...which you commissioned and somehow
failed to turn over to my office.

00:23:58.375 --> 00:24:00.167
- I've no time for this.
- I think you do.

00:24:00.375 --> 00:24:02.167
Allow me to summarize what you know.

00:24:02.375 --> 00:24:05.792
The Heights are seismologically unsound,
the whole area is uninsurable.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.958
- It's worthless.
- As is your theory.

00:24:09.167 --> 00:24:11.583
There's no way
you'd have gotten a building permit.

00:24:11.792 --> 00:24:13.792
- And you knew that.
- What do you want, Sandy?

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.208
I wanna buy back the Heights.

00:24:16.417 --> 00:24:18.000
For a dollar.

00:24:19.625 --> 00:24:21.625
You cannot be serious.

00:24:23.792 --> 00:24:25.875
Merry Christmas.

00:24:28.833 --> 00:24:31.667
So are you ready for your present?

00:24:31.833 --> 00:24:35.250
Yeah, I'm ready. Hand me the keys.
I'll learn to drive stick eventually.

00:24:35.458 --> 00:24:37.583
Very funny, Seth.
Always have to ruin the mood.

00:24:37.792 --> 00:24:38.833
That's what I do.

00:24:39.917 --> 00:24:41.292
Ready?

00:24:49.542 --> 00:24:52.542
The Adventures of Seth Cohen
and Captain Oats.

00:24:52.750 --> 00:24:54.792
Volume 1: "Confidence."

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:57.750
- You made this?
- No, I bought it on eBay.

00:24:57.958 --> 00:25:00.458
I can't believe you did this.
This is amazing.

00:25:01.625 --> 00:25:04.583
Hey, this Seth in the story
seems really handsome and awesome.

00:25:04.792 --> 00:25:09.083
- I guess I took some liberties.
- You dumbed him down a little bit.

00:25:18.458 --> 00:25:20.625
- This is fantastic.
- Thanks.

00:25:21.875 --> 00:25:25.458
- So how's Seth doing?
- He's fine, I think.

00:25:25.667 --> 00:25:28.958
It's hard to tell
with him sometimes. Why?

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.417
Does he ever do things that sort of...

00:25:33.625 --> 00:25:36.792
...make you question yourself
as a parent?

00:25:38.292 --> 00:25:42.417
Well, there was the model home
and Tijuana...

00:25:42.625 --> 00:25:44.083
...and a thing with the Range Rover...

00:25:44.292 --> 00:25:46.958
...and an IMAX movie that
I didn't quite buy.

00:25:47.167 --> 00:25:51.125
But they're kids. I mean, they do stuff.
They get in trouble, right?

00:25:51.333 --> 00:25:54.292
Our parents would've had a heart attack
if they knew what we did.

00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:59.083
Come on, we were good kids.
We were. Weren't we?

00:25:59.292 --> 00:26:01.083
- We were good kids.
- Yeah.

00:26:01.292 --> 00:26:03.875
And we have good kids.

00:26:44.125 --> 00:26:46.458
Okay, hang on for a second.
What are we doing here?

00:26:46.667 --> 00:26:49.833
Because Anna went to get drinks.
She'll be back in, like, one second.

00:26:50.042 --> 00:26:52.083
- Come here.
- Why?

00:26:52.292 --> 00:26:53.750
- Just come here.
- Okay.

00:26:55.875 --> 00:26:57.167
Stay there.

00:27:06.042 --> 00:27:07.917
I hear you like comic books, Cohen.

00:27:08.542 --> 00:27:10.417
This is true.

00:27:14.542 --> 00:27:16.667
Merry Christmas.

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.667
Good Lord, I think I'm gonna pass out.

00:27:30.458 --> 00:27:34.000
- You're not going anywhere.
- Okay.

00:27:40.292 --> 00:27:42.875
- Yes?
- What's this?

00:27:43.625 --> 00:27:45.458
That's Anna's present.
She made it for me.

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:48.667
- She made it?
- Yeah.

00:27:49.125 --> 00:27:50.750
It's amazing.

00:27:50.958 --> 00:27:53.792
I know, but your present's amazing too.
It's really amazing.

00:27:55.292 --> 00:27:57.125
Hey, there you...

00:27:57.333 --> 00:27:58.792
...are.

00:27:59.625 --> 00:28:03.083
Hey, Anna, Summer was just
giving me her gift. It's cool.

00:28:03.292 --> 00:28:06.583
- You're Wonder Woman?
- Yeah. So?

00:28:06.833 --> 00:28:08.833
I mean, you look...

00:28:09.042 --> 00:28:10.833
...amazing.

00:28:11.042 --> 00:28:12.958
Is that my story?

00:28:14.458 --> 00:28:18.917
My God, I made you a comic book.
What am I, 8?

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:21.375
Way to go, Wonder Whore.

00:28:21.583 --> 00:28:23.583
Hey, Wonder Woman's not
a whore, okay? Stop.

00:28:23.792 --> 00:28:26.125
- What are we doing?
- I don't know, this is nuts.

00:28:26.333 --> 00:28:27.958
Hold up, you guys, one second.

00:28:28.167 --> 00:28:31.167
Let's not have one speed bump
derail the whole train, okay?

00:28:31.375 --> 00:28:33.917
Let's not throw the baby out
with the bath water.

00:28:34.625 --> 00:28:36.500
- Let's make some more metaphors.
- Look...

00:28:36.708 --> 00:28:41.542
...I'm not into talking about, like,
feelings or whatever...

00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:42.917
...but I like you.

00:28:43.125 --> 00:28:45.417
Okay, and so does she.

00:28:47.333 --> 00:28:50.750
- Lf we don't put an end to this soon...
- Someone's gonna get hurt.

00:28:52.292 --> 00:28:53.500
You gotta choose, Cohen.

00:29:08.375 --> 00:29:10.167
Did you miss me?

00:29:10.583 --> 00:29:13.417
- Come on, let's dance.
- You know how I feel about dancing.

00:29:13.583 --> 00:29:16.333
You know how I don't care.
Come on, it's a party.

00:29:16.500 --> 00:29:18.292
Yeah, an office party.

00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:22.708
I thought you wanted to have fun.
Don't make me make you have fun.

00:29:24.292 --> 00:29:26.250
I'm guessing that's not eggnog.

00:29:26.458 --> 00:29:30.667
So what? Come on, if you don't wanna
dance we could just get out of here.

00:29:30.833 --> 00:29:35.500
- I didn't see you with a cocktail.
- Well, maybe I brought my own.

00:29:35.708 --> 00:29:37.417
Want some?

00:29:38.250 --> 00:29:39.625
What's going on with you today?

00:29:40.458 --> 00:29:43.458
- What's the big deal? You drink.
- Not alone in the bathroom.

00:29:43.625 --> 00:29:45.000
I'm just having fun.

00:29:45.208 --> 00:29:47.583
When I met you,
you were passed out in your driveway.

00:29:47.792 --> 00:29:50.167
Then it was an alley in Mexico. It's like...

00:29:50.375 --> 00:29:51.917
It's like my mom all over again.

00:29:52.250 --> 00:29:54.292
Shut up.

00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:56.750
- We're getting out of here.
- No, I am.

00:29:56.958 --> 00:29:58.500
- Enjoy the party.
- You can't drive.

00:29:58.708 --> 00:30:03.167
Get your hands off of me. I have enough
people in my life telling me what to do.

00:30:05.333 --> 00:30:07.167
See you.

00:30:19.375 --> 00:30:21.333
- Come on, let me drive.
- Get away from me.

00:30:21.625 --> 00:30:22.750
Hey.

00:30:22.958 --> 00:30:24.417
Hey.

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:27.375
I'm fine.

00:30:46.625 --> 00:30:50.458
And so, effective immediately,
I'm transferring the title of the Heights...

00:30:50.667 --> 00:30:54.000
...to the Balboa Land Trust
for the very reasonable price...

00:30:54.208 --> 00:30:55.583
...of $ 1.

00:31:00.292 --> 00:31:04.083
And I couldn't have done it without
the help of my son-in-law, Sandy Cohen.

00:31:07.167 --> 00:31:10.792
Thanks, Cal. But I can't take credit
for this. You did this all on your own.

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.667
To Caleb Nichol, the most generous
man in Newport Beach.

00:31:15.542 --> 00:31:17.750
Thanks.

00:31:22.875 --> 00:31:24.958
Happy Hanukkah, Sandy.

00:31:47.833 --> 00:31:49.458
- Great.
- What? You're driving.

00:31:49.667 --> 00:31:52.333
- Yeah, because you're drunk.
- I'm not...

00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:55.208
Fine.

00:32:00.208 --> 00:32:02.208
- Where is it?
- Come on, put it away.

00:32:02.417 --> 00:32:04.250
- I'm trying.
- I'm still on probation.

00:32:04.458 --> 00:32:06.667
I said, I'm trying.

00:32:13.333 --> 00:32:15.583
Of course this is happening.

00:32:18.583 --> 00:32:20.458
Oh, God.

00:32:35.083 --> 00:32:38.792
Happy holidays. License. Registration.

00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:41.542
You got a broken tail light,
you know that?

00:32:41.750 --> 00:32:43.458
It just happened. I'll get it fixed.

00:32:44.708 --> 00:32:47.542
- You kids haven't been drinking?
- No, sir.

00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:55.167
- Everything all right here, miss?
- Yeah, fine. Thanks.

00:32:57.500 --> 00:32:59.083
- Miss, would you...?
- We got a 459...

00:32:59.292 --> 00:33:01.042
... at 1508 Cornwall Lane
in West Cliff.

00:33:01.250 --> 00:33:03.417
All cars in the area
please respond immediately.

00:33:03.917 --> 00:33:05.750
Copy that.

00:33:05.958 --> 00:33:08.083
I've got a call I need to get to.

00:33:08.292 --> 00:33:12.250
I'm gonna let you go with just a warning
for that tail light. You get that fixed.

00:33:12.458 --> 00:33:14.292
- Drive straight home.
- Yes, sir.

00:33:41.125 --> 00:33:42.958
Stop, okay? You're scaring me.

00:33:43.167 --> 00:33:45.583
Good. You're scaring me.

00:33:50.750 --> 00:33:54.958
There's drinking, crying, cops.
Well, it must be Christmas.

00:34:11.958 --> 00:34:14.083
I left this behind.

00:34:15.167 --> 00:34:16.625
I am not doing it again.

00:34:19.167 --> 00:34:20.750
Okay.

00:34:29.875 --> 00:34:31.625
Okay.

00:34:48.292 --> 00:34:50.375
Well, the ladies laid down the law.
It's over.

00:34:50.583 --> 00:34:53.042
- What are you gonna do?
- I have no idea.

00:34:53.250 --> 00:34:56.667
I don't know. No female's
ever really offered me a choice.

00:34:56.875 --> 00:34:59.875
I really only know
how to handle rejection and ridicule.

00:35:00.042 --> 00:35:03.250
I have a really good handle on ridicule.
How was your night?

00:35:04.500 --> 00:35:08.458
Marissa got drunk, and we got pulled over
by the cops with an open bottle of vodka.

00:35:08.667 --> 00:35:11.500
Hey, that Marissa's really
making life interesting for you.

00:35:11.667 --> 00:35:14.583
- Yeah. We got in a fight.
- What about the cop?

00:35:14.792 --> 00:35:19.583
Got a radio call. Let us off
with a warning for a busted tail light.

00:35:19.792 --> 00:35:23.250
- Now you see why I hate Christmas.
- Hang on a second, Ryan.

00:35:23.458 --> 00:35:28.417
It seems to me that what we have here
is a Chrismukkah miracle.

00:35:28.625 --> 00:35:32.167
Thank you. Think about it for a second.
The old Ryan, what would've happened?

00:35:32.375 --> 00:35:36.167
He would've got busted. For sure. But
this time, you had Jesus working for you.

00:35:36.375 --> 00:35:38.750
And you had Moses.
Working together. The super team.

00:35:38.958 --> 00:35:42.417
Fighting for you, to keep you safe
and give you a second chance.

00:35:42.625 --> 00:35:44.417
Touched by an angel.

00:35:44.625 --> 00:35:48.667
That's nice. It's got a good ring to it.
I believe my faith has been restored.

00:35:49.458 --> 00:35:50.750
I should go get ready.

00:35:50.958 --> 00:35:53.708
- Anna will be here soon.
- What are you going to tell her?

00:35:53.917 --> 00:35:55.750
I'm sure the words will come.

00:35:56.458 --> 00:35:59.917
All right, I just think that...

00:36:00.125 --> 00:36:02.500
...considering everything...
Actually, wait, hang on.

00:36:02.708 --> 00:36:05.625
Let me actually try another approach.

00:36:05.792 --> 00:36:10.292
I think you're awesome,
and you're hilarious, and you're caliente.

00:36:10.875 --> 00:36:14.917
And I think, you know,
you're extremely witty, and you're wise...

00:36:15.125 --> 00:36:18.750
...and I kind of can't believe
I'm actually gonna say this.

00:36:19.208 --> 00:36:21.125
But...

00:36:21.333 --> 00:36:23.792
...actually, I think
we should be friends.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:27.167
And I want you to have this.

00:36:27.375 --> 00:36:28.917
I don't wanna be your friend.

00:36:32.917 --> 00:36:34.833
I don't wanna be your friend.

00:36:42.542 --> 00:36:45.375
You can never have
too many copies of The Goonies.

00:37:00.042 --> 00:37:02.500
That was corporate espionage.
I could've fired you.

00:37:02.708 --> 00:37:04.375
Even sued you for breach
of confidentiality.

00:37:04.583 --> 00:37:08.458
Dad. You were extorting the county,
putting the company at huge risks.

00:37:08.667 --> 00:37:10.708
One day this was gonna come out.
Then what?

00:37:10.917 --> 00:37:15.125
When you found that report,
you could've shown me.

00:37:15.333 --> 00:37:17.375
You could've shown me
when it started.

00:37:17.583 --> 00:37:19.708
I'm sorry, but I just didn't see
any other way.

00:37:19.917 --> 00:37:25.417
It was dishonest,
calculating and ruthless. Kiki...

00:37:25.750 --> 00:37:28.292
...we just might make
a real-estate mogul out of you yet.

00:37:30.250 --> 00:37:32.208
Well, that's something to look forward to.

00:37:36.583 --> 00:37:39.542
Your mom's ornaments.
The tree looks nice.

00:37:40.917 --> 00:37:43.583
There may be a gift under there for you.

00:37:44.292 --> 00:37:45.750
Maybe.

00:37:47.458 --> 00:37:50.792
Hey, where you going?
We were thinking about getting a movie.

00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:52.875
Marissa's going to see her therapist.

00:37:53.083 --> 00:37:56.083
- She's going through a lot.
- Yeah, I thought I'd go with her.

00:37:56.875 --> 00:37:58.833
Yeah, you could...

00:37:59.042 --> 00:38:01.042
...or not.

00:38:02.875 --> 00:38:07.583
Marissa's gonna have to figure this
out by herself, and you gotta let her.

00:38:08.667 --> 00:38:11.708
You're here with us now.
You don't have to be the parent anymore.

00:38:15.458 --> 00:38:18.458
- A movie, huh?
- Yeah, but it's my pick.

00:38:18.667 --> 00:38:21.667
The selection of a movie
is something of an art.

00:39:00.750 --> 00:39:04.625
I came here three times before I
actually walked through that door.

00:39:08.417 --> 00:39:11.417
I know you. You go to Harbor, right?

00:39:12.292 --> 00:39:14.333
Marissa Cooper. Hi.

00:39:14.750 --> 00:39:19.417
You're the girl at school who
organizes things. Parties and stuff, right?

00:39:20.292 --> 00:39:22.583
Social chair is what that's called.

00:39:30.083 --> 00:39:34.292
- You go to Harbor?
- No. No, I go to Pacific.

00:39:34.625 --> 00:39:36.167
Oliver Trask.

00:39:39.833 --> 00:39:44.958
For a social chair... Well, I don't
find you to be very social at all.

00:39:45.167 --> 00:39:48.292
Gonna have to talk
to somebody about a recall.

00:39:48.500 --> 00:39:53.208
This is a psychiatrist's office.
It's kind of embarrassing.

00:39:53.417 --> 00:39:57.833
Yeah. Yeah, you're right.
This is totally embarrassing.

00:39:58.500 --> 00:40:01.792
So let's address the obvious and move on.

00:40:02.667 --> 00:40:04.875
What's wrong with you?

00:40:09.625 --> 00:40:12.208
What is wrong with you?

00:40:13.750 --> 00:40:16.333
Well, if I knew, I wouldn't be here.

00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:22.167
You're not an alcoholic yet.

00:40:22.375 --> 00:40:23.833
You've OD'd at least once.

00:40:24.458 --> 00:40:28.125
Pills, I'd say.
Muscle relaxants, definitely.

00:40:32.917 --> 00:40:34.292
Painkillers.

00:40:35.583 --> 00:40:37.542
You didn't really want to hurt yourself.

00:40:37.750 --> 00:40:40.708
Kurt Cobain, yeah,
he wanted to hurt himself.

00:40:43.750 --> 00:40:45.917
You know, coming here wasn't my idea.

00:40:46.667 --> 00:40:50.625
Maybe not. But you wouldn't be here
if you didn't want to be.

00:40:51.875 --> 00:40:54.458
You want to know
why you are the way you are.

00:40:59.125 --> 00:41:01.958
That's you. I'm waiting on the next door.

00:41:04.208 --> 00:41:06.125
See you next week.

00:41:17.417 --> 00:41:19.417
How did it go with the girls?

00:41:19.625 --> 00:41:23.250
- Seth Cohen starter pack?
- I think I'm past that now.

00:41:25.917 --> 00:41:28.375
- Is that what I think it is?
- Figured I'd hang it.

00:41:28.917 --> 00:41:32.125
All right, man,
another Chrismukkah convert.

00:41:32.333 --> 00:41:33.333
Nice.

00:41:33.542 --> 00:41:37.958
I never doubted it for a second. Check it
out, I already put the hook up just in case.

00:41:40.125 --> 00:41:42.958
- Hey.
- All right, what'll it be?

00:41:43.167 --> 00:41:45.417
Fiddler on the Roof,
It's a Wonderful Life...

00:41:45.625 --> 00:41:48.458
...or my selection,
Sylvester Stallone's Over the Top.

00:41:48.625 --> 00:41:52.458
- Isn't that the arm-wrestling movie?
- Arm-wrestling classic.

00:41:52.667 --> 00:41:58.000
- Hey, merry Chrismukkah, you guys.
- Thank you.
